{0 Observe Unix}

[observe-unix] supplies the Unix implementation of [Observe.Platform.S]. It
provides the OS wall clock, passive terminal capability detection, and exact
console writes to standard error without
selecting a runtime.

The platform selects truecolor, 256-color, 16-color, or plain presentation from
passive terminal signals. Redirected output, [NO_COLOR], an absent or empty
[TERM], [TERM=dumb], and probe failure remain plain. Console writes are
synchronous, so a slow destination
can delay the caller.

Use {!module:Observe_unix.Platform} with [Observe.Runtime.Make] for a
custom composition. Lwt applications can use the ready [observe-lwt-unix]
package.
